## Scrolling

When the panel is shorter than its contents, only the commit notes scroll. Its header, the branch with Pull and Push, stays at its top, and the summary stays beneath it; the message box, Generate, and Commit stay fixed along its bottom, always in view, however many notes there are. The notes, between the summary and the message box, fill what is left and scroll within it, with a [Scrollbar](../scrollbar/index.md#scrollbar) along their right only while they overflow. While the scrollbar shows, there are 6 pixels of the body's own colour between the notes' right edge and the scrollbar's left, so no note's box ever touches the scrollbar or runs its colour into the scrollbar's border: the notes narrow by the scrollbar's width and that gap, rewrapping, and widen back to the body's padding when it goes. The scrollbar sits in the body's right padding, against the panel's right edge. Everything else is always as tall as it needs, so shrinking the panel takes room from the notes first, down to nothing; only once the notes have no room left does the rest give way, the summary last before the header. The body's colour runs all the way down the panel.

